WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.978 --> 00:00:05.379
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:13.110
This is our robotic garden.

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:16.260
The inspiration behind
it was that there

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:18.570
isn't a lot of
interest, especially

00:00:18.570 --> 00:00:20.640
from young girls
in computer science

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:23.850
and not a great way for
them to get interested.

00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:26.910
And the garden is a
great way to teach

00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:30.210
some of these basic concepts
in a visually pleasing way.

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:38.940
We have over 100 different
robotic flowers in this garden.

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:40.520
And they can all open and close.

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:44.240
And the LED-lit flowers
can also change colors.

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:47.540
So we can show distributed
algorithms running

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:49.700
on the garden as
well and demonstrate

00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:52.370
some basic algorithm
concepts for beginning

00:00:52.370 --> 00:00:53.930
computer scientists.

00:00:53.930 --> 00:00:57.080
You can interact with the
garden through the computer.

00:00:57.080 --> 00:01:00.350
We have an interface that shows
the garden split up into tiles.

00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:03.200
And you can click on a
tile and click on a color

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:05.990
and the flowers on that
tile will change colors

00:01:05.990 --> 00:01:08.600
or you can make them
inflate or deflate.

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:11.030
And we also have buttons
to display the distributed

00:01:11.030 --> 00:01:13.942
algorithms that can
run in the garden.

00:01:13.942 --> 00:01:17.790
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:01:22.610 --> 00:01:24.200
One of the more
interesting algorithms

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:27.350
that we can run on the garden
is called graph coloring.

00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:29.420
And so what happens
in graphic coloring

00:01:29.420 --> 00:01:32.540
is every tile will
have flowers that

00:01:32.540 --> 00:01:34.520
are a different color
from the flowers

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:36.260
on every tile around it.

00:01:36.260 --> 00:01:39.380
And we need at most 4 colors
to accomplish this here.

00:01:44.490 --> 00:01:47.370
Recently we displayed the
garden at the Hour of Code.

00:01:47.370 --> 00:01:50.730
And we had some local
high school students

00:01:50.730 --> 00:01:52.020
come and try out the garden.

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:55.050
And then when they saw the
code run in the garden,

00:01:55.050 --> 00:01:56.370
kids were really excited.

00:01:56.370 --> 00:01:58.290
And one of the
really neat things

00:01:58.290 --> 00:02:00.660
that happened as a result
of the Hour of Code

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:03.150
was I had a couple of
kids come up and ask me

00:02:03.150 --> 00:02:06.270
where they could get their
own components to make

00:02:06.270 --> 00:02:09.037
their own robotic systems
and how to get started.

00:02:09.037 --> 00:02:11.370
And so it really was doing
what we were hoping it would,

00:02:11.370 --> 00:02:13.740
which is inspiring
kids to get interested

00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:16.530
in robotics and programming.

00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:20.480
[MUSIC PLAYING]

